A||N||8||FieroSTETZ||87GT stumbles! (or misses?)||||1||
Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||10-19-2000||10:19 AM||||recently while driving my beloved 87GT, I noticed that while driving a constant speed that the engine seemed to be booming, very muted popping noise, and the tach needle would jump around. I am getting no error codes whatsoever, and recently checked and regapped all my plugs. anyone have any ideas? My ignition coil is fairly new (5 mos.) but it already is looking kinda sorry. any help would be greatly appreciated!||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||10-19-2000||12:44 PM||||First guess would have to be the tach filter is going bad.  The tach filter looks like a condenser and is located near the distributor.  Unplug it and drive the car without it plugged in (you lose the tach, for the duration of this experiment).<P>If the stumbling/missing goes away, you've found the problem.  You need a Rodney Dickman replacement.  Hope that turns out to be the problem, because it's easy to fix.  Good luck!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||3
Z||000002||FieroSTETZ||10-19-2000||02:01 PM||||is there any way someone could send me a pic or drawing of the tach filter and its location? my car's wiring harness was modified by the previous owner. i think that may be the problem, because when i bought the car the original tach was disconnected, and an aftermarket one was installed on the a- pillar. all there shenanigans started about 3 weeks after i removed the aftermarket one and re connected the original one. i am looking in there, and theres a little canister, looks screwed in, behind the distributor, about an inch thick. is that the filter? ||||reg||5
Z||000003||mrfixit58||10-19-2000||02:54 PM||||The tach filter is usually mounted at the base of the coil on the heat shield between the coil and the motor. It looks like an old style condensor (as in points and condensor). The shape is cylindrical, about 3/4 inch in diameter and 1 1/2 inch long. <P>I had the same thing going on when I bought my 87 GT. The problem turned out to be a bad pick-up coil in the distributor. The way I found it is one day, it would not start (which is typical when they go bad  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ). After I replaced the coil, all the sputtering went away. Go figure. Anyway, it's something else to try if you don't have any luck with the tach filter.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000004||FieroSTETZ||10-19-2000||03:28 PM||||well, my fears were realized- my car has had the tach filter removed, there is no tach filter on the car anymore. i had my dad help me out with reassembling the wiring harness getting rid of the shoddy wiring and stuff from the stereo equipment, that thing said "radio filter" or something. was judged to be unimportant, so it was taken off. what do I do now?||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfixit58||10-19-2000||05:49 PM||||Rody Dickman sells replacement units (albeit not origial). Check:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/</A> <P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000006||FieroSTETZ||10-21-2000||03:15 PM||||well, i seem to have the problem nailed! it looks as if the previous owner mounted the ignition coil directly to the engine with thick SS brackets, giving it no shock protection. i plugged a timing light onto the wire from the distrimbutor to the coil and noticed that when the car stumbled, the light would skip a beat or two. so, i went out and bougt an msd ignition coil, gm HEI style (plugs right in like stock!) and now i have put about 26 trouble free miles on it, with better mileage, too! the only thing that bothers me is that my car still doesn't have a tach filter, but does not seem to be missing it at all? how could this be?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460599&p=25516673"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||JetroGT||10-22-2000||02:34 AM||||Sorry about the quality of the picture. Here is a partial diagram of the ignition system showing the tach filter. I hope this helps.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blockdiagram.jpg"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||StuGood||10-22-2000||02:56 PM||||Tach filter cleans up the input for the stock tachometer.  Engine doesn't need the filter to run right, but a bad tach filter  <B>can</B> make the engine run wrong.<P>Me comprendes, Mendez? ||||reg||1
